## Inventory Fills Fast — Fish Don't Stack

Each raw fish takes its own inventory slot (no stacking), and at 8x speed a
full 28-slot inventory fills in well under a minute of continuous net fishing.
Inventory becoming full silently stalls XP gain (you stop catching), which
tanked our XP rate in testing. Drop unneeded starting gear (axe, tools,
weapons, runes) immediately to maximize free slots, then in the fishing loop,
proactively drop all non-kept items (keep just the net + 1 food) once free
slots drop to ~2:

```typescript
const inv = sdk.getInventory();
const freeSlots = 28 - inv.length;
if (freeSlots <= 2) {
    for (const item of inv) {
        if (!KEEP.has(item.name.toLowerCase())) {
            await sdk.sendDropItem(item.slot);
        }
    }
    continue;
}
```

This pattern (Draynor Net/Bait spot, dropping fish on the ground) sustained
~310-340 XP/min peak rate (per `check_xp_rate.ts`) with continuous full-HP
